# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# (gitignore has NO end-of-line comments — a pattern plus trailing text matches
# nothing, which silently un-ignored these files. Comments live on their own
# lines; never append them to a pattern.)
config/api_keys.json
#   your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/certs/
#   the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/whatsapp_web/
#   a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
#   account, not just a key
**/token*.json
#   Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/client_secret*.json
#   Google OAuth client secrets
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*
.hf_token
jarvisd.json
**/agents.json
dashboard_auth.json
# Phase 3 stores (local mode: data_root() is the repo root). The push action
# secret and the VAPID private key live in here — never commit them.
scheduler.json
scheduler_logs/
tasks.json
tasks/
# The lead CRM (local mode: data_root() is the repo root). -wal/-shm are SQLite
# sidecars that appear whenever a read is in flight.
crm.sqlite
crm.sqlite-wal
crm.sqlite-shm
push_vapid.json
push_subscriptions.json
push_action_secret
# Phase 4e display artifacts (local mode: data_root() is the repo root). These
# are model-written pages saved to disk — runtime output, not source.
display/
# Phase 4d mail idempotency ledger: Message-IDs of everything we ever sent.
mail_ledger.json
# Parked phone-sensor store.
phone/
# Every runtime key file lands in config/; the two named above are the ones
# that are not per-plugin credentials.
config/*.json
uploads/

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# Dropped media (videos/screenshots the user hands over) — never commit
.inbox/

# E2E runtime
e2e/data/
e2e/data_*/
e2e/hud.png
godseye/_server/node_modules/

# The vendored God's Eye View: its BUILT app must be committed, or the Space
# image has sources and nothing to serve. The generic dist/ and build/ rules
# above were silently eating godseye/_server/{dist,build} — 430 files, the
# entire application, gone from the image while the build still went green.
!godseye/_server/dist/
!godseye/_server/build/
godseye/_server/.gev-logs/

# Phase 6 knowledge store (local mode: data_root() is the repo root)
knowledge.sqlite
knowledge.sqlite-wal
knowledge.sqlite-shm

# local build cache for the globe, regenerated by tools/build-dist.mjs
godseye/_server/.dist-static.json

# coder undo snapshots — runtime state, never source
undo/

# The approval audit trail. Written by core/policy.py to the data root, and it
# lands in the repository when JARVIS_DATA is unset — which is what a test run
# does. Runtime state, never source.
audit.jsonl
*.sqlite
